# Secrets — the Stratz API key lives in .env and must never be committed.
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Runtime data: API caches, captured frames, debug output, downloaded assets.
data_cache/
captures/
debug_out/
assets/portraits/
assets/items/
assets/synth/
assets/gate/
assets/role_icons/
# SCREENSHOTS OF THE GAME ARE VALVE'S ARTWORK, like everything above.
# This folder is where the resolution sweep is pointed, so it fills up
# with full-screen captures of the draft - and it was the one artwork
# folder NOT listed here, which is the way that rule gets broken by
# accident rather than by decision. A frame also shows whatever else was
# on screen and the player names in the game, so it carries more than
# the artwork does.
assets/screenshots/
# The app icon: whatever the user chose, and the .ico written
# from it for the shortcut and the taskbar pin.
assets/app.ico
assets/app.png
assets/app.jpg
assets/app.jpeg
assets/app.bmp
assets/app-generated.ico
calibration_local.json

# OS / editor
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
ui_settings.json
preferences.json
# Which accounts the match history analyser has looked at. Local only, so
# a copy of this app carries nobody's account numbers or results.
history_accounts.json
# Workbooks the analyser exported.
history_reports/

# Recording sessions: payloads, frames and state logs from real games.
# EVERYTHING WORTH SENDING, under one folder: the setup transcript,
# crash tracebacks, recorded sessions and the zips that were mailed.
# See `draft_assist/debugdir.py`.
debug/
# Where the recordings and the scratch pictures lived before they moved
# in. Kept ignored so an install that has not been opened since the
# change does not suddenly offer them up.
recordings/

# Which release this install is on, written by tools/update_app.py when a
# downloaded copy updates itself. It describes THIS machine, not the app.
installed_version.json

# The last run for each account the analyser has measured. Local only,
# beside history_accounts.json: a copy of this app carries nobody else's
# match history.
history_cache/
assets/tick-generated.png

# The single-instance lock (see `ui/single.py`) — a PID, written at
# startup and removed on the way out.
running.lock

# The console-free front door the app writes beside the launcher at
# every start (see appicon.folder_link). Local, per machine, never ours
# to commit.
*.lnk

# The app's own Python packages, kept beside it so a repair or a
# copied folder installs with no download. Never committed: the ZIP
# updater fetches every tracked file, and these are 181 MB against the
# app's own ~2 MB. See tools/stock_wheels.py.
wheels/

# The shareable zip `tools/make_release.py` builds: the app plus every
# package it runs on, about 240 MB. A build output, and the one thing
# that must never be committed for the same reason `wheels/` is not.
dist/
